<title>FRANCE: Total sees rise in operating income.</title>
<headline>Total sees rise in operating income.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total's chief executive officer Thierry Desmarest said on Wednesday he expects an increase in operating income of four billion francs over the three years up to and including 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;For the next three years, and with unchanged circumstances, we aim to improve the operating results by four billion francs,&quot; he told a news conference called to announce the company's 1996 results.</p>
<p>Estimated gross operating income before charges in 1996 was 10.7 billion francs, the company said.</p>
